   "resumo_en": "Motörhead is the debut studio album by English heavy metal band Motörhead. It was released on 12 August 1977 by pub rock and early punk rock label Chiswick Records, one of the first for the label, and the band's only release under Chiswick. The album contains the line-up of Lemmy Kilmister on bass and vocals, \"Fast\" Eddie Clarke on lead guitar, and Philthy Animal Taylor on drums.  The sleeve artwork featured the debut of Snaggletooth, the War-Pig, the fanged face logo created by artist Joe Petagno that would become an icon of the band.\nAn earlier album, On Parole, was recorded in 1975–76 for United Artists, but was released only in November 1979.",
