   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/On_Parole",
   "resumo_en": "On Parole is a studio recording released by the original line-up of English rock band Motörhead, which at the time consisted of Lemmy Kilmister on vocals and bass, Larry Wallis on guitar, and Phil \"Philthy Animal\" Taylor on drums (replacing Lucas Fox). It was intended as their first album and left unreleased at the time of its completion in 1976, and it was not released until over three years later, in November 1979, after the commercial success of Overkill and Bomber that same year. It was released without the band's permission, and they consequently distanced themselves from it. As a result, it was not considered an official release by the band at the time and they did not want it released, as they had moved on, since then, first to Chiswick Records and then to Bronze Records. The LP entered the UK charts on 8 December, where it peaked at No. 65.\nWith guitarist \"Fast\" Eddie Clarke replacing Larry Wallis in March 1976, most of On Parole's songs were re-recorded in April 1977, and formed the band's official first album, Motörhead, released the same year.",
