   "resumo_en": "Sacrifice is the twelfth studio album by British rock band Motörhead. It was released on 27 March 1995 via SPV/Steamhammer, the band's first release on the label. It is the second and final album to feature the four-piece lineup of Lemmy, Phil Campbell, Würzel, and Mikkey Dee, as Würzel left the band after the album's recording. It is also the last album to feature any four-piece band lineup as they would revert back to a trio-lineup starting with Overnight Sensation (1996)",
